Description: Fix Python 3 incompatibilities in the font tweak scripts
 The scripts run by the sfd Makefile to adjust the generated fonts
 (set_isFixedPitch, correct_fsSelection and their support modules in
 tools/generate/tweeks) still contained Python 2 idioms and raised
 exceptions under Python 3.  This went unnoticed for a long time
 because the make output is piped through "tail", which masked the
 non-zero exit status of the failing commands.
 .
 Fixes:
  * OpenType/table.py: namedtuple instances have no __dict__, use the
    namedtuple API (_fields, getattr, _replace) instead.
  * OpenType/checksum.py: indexing a bytes object yields int on
    Python 3, so do not call ord() on the result.
  * OpenType/typeutils.py: panose_str() now handles a bytes value.
  * set_isFixedPitch.py: exit successfully for non-monospaced faces
    (the tweak does not apply to them), and write the font buffer as
    bytes.
  * correct_fsSelection.py: write the font buffer as bytes.
  * use a python3 shebang; the unversioned "python" interpreter is not
    installed in the build environment.
Author: Bastian Germann <bage@debian.org>
Forwarded: no
---
